[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0001
TITLE: Instruction to structured task
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall convert a natural-language bridge inspection instruction into a task record with target element, location tag, defect classes and required views, and shall reject any output that does not conform to the task schema.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The inspection workflow requires machine-checkable tasks; free text cannot be scheduled or audited.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Accuracy is reported per field over a fixed, versioned instruction set; schema violations are counted and retained with raw model outputs.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0002
TITLE: Image to structured finding
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
Given an image and a task record, the system shall produce a structured finding containing defect class, image region, confidence and an explicit abstain flag.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Downstream reporting needs machine-readable findings and an explicit uncertainty channel.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Findings are evaluated on a named public or synthetic dataset whose licence is recorded; per-class results and abstention rate are reported.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0003
TITLE: Local GPU model execution
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall execute the selected vision-language or language models on the development GPU in PyTorch and record model identifier, precision, library versions and device identifier for every run.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deployment and PyTorch experience is a stated requirement of the target role; provenance of each run is required for fair comparison.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A run record contains all listed fields and the model produces output for the fixed evaluation set.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0004
TITLE: Latency and resource profiling
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The profiling harness shall measure inference latency distribution, peak memory and, where the platform exposes it, energy, using warm-up, repeated runs and raw per-run output.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Placement decisions depend on measured cost; summary statistics without raw data cannot be audited.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
The harness reproduces its raw output format on the same host; summaries are computed only from retained raw files.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0005
TITLE: Task placement decision
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
Given a task record, device profiles and link state, the system shall select one placement from onboard, edge server, cloud or split inference, using a deterministic function of its declared inputs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Placement across onboard, edge and cloud is the central systems question of the target role.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Identical inputs yield identical placements; the function is compared against fixed-placement and greedy-latency baselines on the same replay.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0006
TITLE: Fallback under link or budget violation
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
When the link is degraded or lost, or a measured budget is exceeded, the system shall select a fallback placement and log the trigger and the decision.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A placement policy without an explicit fallback is not safe to evaluate under realistic network conditions.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Injected link-loss and budget-violation events in a replay produce the logged fallback decision in every injected case.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0007
TITLE: Reproducible scenario replay
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall replay task streams with synthetic network and battery traces from recorded seeds, producing identical event logs for identical inputs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Comparisons between placement policies are only meaningful under identical inputs.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Two replays with the same seed and configuration produce byte-identical event logs.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0008
TITLE: Result provenance
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
Every reported result shall identify code revision, configuration, seed, host or device identifier, raw artifact location and analysis command.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Results without provenance cannot be reproduced or checked by a reviewer.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Each result record in the repository contains every listed field; records missing a field are rejected by inspection.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: B0-REQ-0024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0009
TITLE: Development-host labelling
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
Measurements taken on the development PC shall be labelled as development-host results and shall not be reported as onboard, edge-device or flight performance.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No edge hardware is available; mislabelled results would overstate the evidence.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Every result document states the host type; inspection finds no onboard or edge-device claim without a corresponding hardware record.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: EDG-REQ-0004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0010
TITLE: Bridge inspection task scope
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall be scoped to civil bridge inspection tasks and shall not include defence, surveillance or targeting functions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The civil-use attribute of the target project is a precondition for the work.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection of task schema and datasets finds no non-civil classes or use cases; dataset licences are recorded.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0011
TITLE: Model execution and profiling scope
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The model execution and profiling capability shall be treated as an optional extension of the platform and shall not depend on B0 control results for its own acceptance.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Keeps the edge-inference track independent of the attitude-control baseline, which is frozen at component level.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
The model and profiling tests run without the B0 control modules installed.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: B0-REQ-0030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0012
TITLE: Placement policy scope
STATUS: deprecated
STATE: planned
STATEMENT: >>>
The placement policy shall be evaluated on replayed scenarios only; no flight, hardware-in-the-loop or live-link claim shall be made without a separately approved extension.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents simulated placement results from being presented as operational evidence.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Inspection of result documents finds only replay-scope claims.
<<<
EVIDENCE: none yet
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: B0-REQ-0030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0034
TITLE: Standardized detector interface
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The detector shall expose an infer(frame) interface independent of ROS 2 and flight-control middleware.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
A synthetic input is checked against the declared output schema without middleware dependencies.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/src/detector.py; edge_inference/tests/test_detector_scaffold.py (synthetic frames and adapter output); edge_inference/README.md describes supported adapters.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0035
TITLE: Lightweight detector baseline
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall establish a lightweight bridge-defect detector baseline using YOLOv8n or YOLO11n and an appropriately licensed public concrete-defect dataset.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Report model, dataset version, licence, split, and per-class detection metrics with retained raw outputs.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/scripts/train_baseline.py; edge_inference/scripts/prepare_codebrim.py; edge_inference/tests/test_prepare_codebrim.py; edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day1_yolov8n_fp32_baseline.md (split and model); Day 3-4 per-class scores are annotation-relative.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0036
TITLE: Structured pruning
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide a structured channel pruning pipeline with configurable sparsity ratios.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Record the pruning configuration, model identity and resulting architecture; verify supported models.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/scripts/compress_pruning.py exposes train --width-ratio and records the ratio and model costs. edge_inference/tests/test_compression_pipeline.py checks physical C2f/Detect widths, parameter counts and synthetic forward passes at 0.5 and 2/3; edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day2_3_pruning_int8_compression.md records the measured default 2/3 model.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0037
TITLE: ONNX and static INT8 quantization
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall export supported models to ONNX and support static INT8 post-training quantization using a declared calibration set.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Record calibration provenance and export configuration; compare outputs on fixed inputs and retain failures.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/scripts/export_fp32_trace.py; edge_inference/scripts/quantize_int8.py; edge_inference/tests/test_compression_pipeline.py (train-only calibration membership and static QDQ round trip); edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day2_3_pruning_int8_compression.md records the calibration and fixed-input comparison.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0038
TITLE: Stage latency profiling
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The profiling pipeline shall measure preprocessing, inference and postprocessing latency, and report mean, P95 and P99.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Retain per-run timing, host identity, warm-up and repetitions; derive summaries from the raw measurements.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/src/benchmark.py; edge_inference/tests/test_detector_scaffold.py (synthetic stage samples and CLI record); edge_inference/scripts/eval_compression_variants.py and edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day2_3_pruning_int8_compression.md (development-host profiles and recorded summaries).

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0039
TITLE: Resource footprint
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The pipeline shall report peak RSS, parameter count, GFLOPs and serialized model size where available.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Record measurement method, units and unsupported quantities without inventing values.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/src/benchmark.py and edge_inference/scripts/eval_compression_variants.py record sampled peak process RSS and serialized size; edge_inference/tests/test_detector_scaffold.py checks both fields. edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day2_3_pruning_int8_compression.md reports these alongside source-architecture parameters and estimated GFLOPs. RSS is not an instantaneous peak or GPU memory.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0040
TITLE: Thread-constrained CPU profile
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The pipeline shall support a declared thread-constrained CPU profile alongside GPU benchmarking.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Report actual host, provider, thread settings and raw timing; do not claim embedded-device performance.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/src/detector.py and edge_inference/scripts/eval_compression_variants.py implement the development-host CPU4 profile (ORT intra-op 4, inter-op 1); edge_inference/tests/test_detector_scaffold.py checks thread options and CLI overrides. edge_inference/logs/2026-11-24_day1_yolov8n_fp32_baseline.md records CPU and GPU reference runs.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EDG-REQ-0041
TITLE: Accuracy and cost frontier
STATUS: approved
STATE: implemented
STATEMENT: >>>
The pipeline shall generate Pareto comparisons of mAP, P95 latency and model size.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Supports a reproducible civil bridge-inspection model-compression and profiling workflow.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE: >>>
Generate from traceable, comparable raw results and record configurations and missing metrics.
<<<
EVIDENCE: edge_inference/scripts/plot_offloading_results.py (pareto) compares cached all-edge descriptive mAP50, standalone CPU4 P95 and ONNX size jointly. edge_inference/tests/test_offloading_experiments.py covers dominance, ties and three-axis trade-offs. edge_inference/docs/technical_note_uav_edge_offloading.md section 3.1 records the four-variant result and coverage limits.
